* L55 COPIA DI BANCO di models/bjt_npn/mje243.lib: modello rinominato Qmje243F, e in fondo le capacita' di
* giunzione ferme a TNOM (script/modelli_banco.py). NON e' un modello del progetto.
* mje243.lib - onsemi MJE243G, NPN complementary silicon power plastic
* transistor, TO-225, 100 V / 4.0 A / 15 W (TC = 25 C).
* VENDOR MODEL, COPIED VERBATIM FROM THE MANUFACTURER'S OWN FILE.
*
* USAGE:
*   .include models/bjt_npn/mje243.lib
*   Q1 collector base emitter Qmje243
*
* NOTE THE MODEL NAME: it is Qmje243, not MJE243. The vendor named it that
* way and it was not "corrected".
*
* Role in this project: NC-056 (L55). CANDIDATE driver-sized replacement
* for the MJE15032 in the Class A emitter follower of the gain block
* (circuits/preamp/gain_block.py:717-718). NOT YET USED BY ANY CIRCUIT: the
* MJE15032/33 stay in the source until the bench of the block (V1, V4,
* PSRR, slew, heat) has been run with this pair and the user has decided.
*
* ------------------------------------------------------------------
* PROVENANCE - the short version. Full record in
* models/bjt_npn/mje243.provenance.json, the freeze in
* vendor/bjt_npn/onsemi/MJE243/PROVENANCE.json, and the sourcing and
* measurements in docs/preamp/data/2026-10-29/L55/modelli/README.md
* ------------------------------------------------------------------
*
* onsemi serves this model at /download/models/lib/mje243.lib (200,
* application/octet-stream, 994 bytes; the check on Content-Type and size is
* the one limitations #18 asks for). The header was read before freezing
* (limitations #20): '.MODEL Qmje243 npn' - the right part. Frozen
* byte-for-byte at vendor/bjt_npn/onsemi/MJE243/mje243.lib and copied here
* unchanged: nothing removed, no value rounded or "corrected".
*
*   diff <(grep -v '^\*' vendor/bjt_npn/onsemi/MJE243/mje243.lib) \
*        <(grep -v '^\*' models/bjt_npn/mje243.lib)   # the KF/AF line only
*
* THE MODEL WAS WRITTEN BY A CONTRACTOR, recorded and not hidden: its own
* header says "Model Generated by MODPEX / Copyright(c) Symmetry Design
* Systems", "Model generated on Jan 22, 03", PSpice format. onsemi
* DISTRIBUTES it as the model of this part, which is what ADR-016 asks for.
*
* ------------------------------------------------------------------
* CROSS-CHECKED AGAINST THE DATASHEET - INSIDE EVERY WINDOW
* ------------------------------------------------------------------
*
* Datasheet MJE243/D, December 2024 Rev. 17, frozen at
* vendor/bjt_npn/onsemi/MJE243/mje243-d.pdf (one document for both
* halves). Conditions read from the RENDERED page 2, not from pdftotext
* (limitations #19). ngspice 47, set temp = 25:
*
*   hFE @ IC = 200 mA, VCE = 1 V     131.128    40 MIN / 180 MAX  inside
*   hFE @ IC = 1.0 A,  VCE = 1 V      56.914    15 MIN            inside
*   fT  @ IC = 100 mA, VCE = 10 V,
*       ftest = 10 MHz                59.933 MHz  40 MHz MIN      inside
*   Cob @ VCB = 10 V, IE = 0, 0.1 MHz 29.154 pF   50 pF MAX        inside
*       (datasheet Fig. 7, typical at 10 V: ~30 pF)
*
* fT is |hfe| x ftest, the gain-bandwidth product AT 10 MHz, which is the
* datasheet's definition (the unity crossing at that bias is higher).
* Recipe: tb_mje243() in scripts/validate_models.py, values locked +-0.5 %.
*
* AT THE FOLLOWER'S OWN POINT, which the datasheet does not specify (the
* project runs ~20 mA, VCE 15 V): hFE 377, Vbe 0.626 V, gm 720 mS,
* Cpi 1.70 nF (of which CJE 0.22 nF at zero bias; the rest is TF x gm),
* Cmu 21 pF, fT 88 MHz (unity crossing). The MJE15032 under the same
* script: hFE 103, Vbe 0.571 V, Cpi 8.09 nF, Cmu 64 pF, fT 12 MHz.
* Note the 55 mV higher Vbe: the Vbe multiplier of the block would have
* to be re-set.
* docs/preamp/data/2026-10-29/L55/modelli/misure.txt
*
* NO FLICKER NOISE FROM THE MANUFACTURER: the vendor card has KF=0 AF=1.
* Since ADR-057 every bipolar carries a declared bound, appended at the
* end of this file.
*
