* L55 (NC-056, ADR-057): FLICKER NOISE ADDED - NOT FROM THE MANUFACTURER
* ------------------------------------------------------------------
* The '+' line at the very end CONTINUES the .MODEL card above: ngspice
* joins it to the last card and skips the comment and blank lines in
* between, and when a parameter repeats the LAST value wins. Measured, not
* assumed, and re-measured on every run by the [flicker] check in
* scripts/validate_models.py (base-current noise, KF read back from
* S(10 Hz) - S(10 kHz)). It sits OUTSIDE the vendor block so that the
* vendor bytes stay exactly as served: the non-comment diff against the
* file under vendor/ is this one line and nothing else.
*
* The numbers are the DECLARED UPPER BOUND of ADR-057 (KF = 1e-13,
* AF = 1.4), the same on every bipolar of the project, not a fit to this
* part: no curve exists for any power bipolar (see models/bjt_npn/
* mje15032.lib for the sources of the bound). The vendor card's own
* KF=0 AF=1 is overridden by the line below.
+ KF=1e-13 AF=1.4
+ TLEVC=1 CTE=0 CTC=0 CTS=0 TVJE=0 TVJC=0 TVJS=0
